EXAM_DATA.papers["2017-english-one"] = {"id":"2017-english-one","year":2017,"label":"2017 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2017-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Could a hug a day keep the doctor away? The answer may be a resounding \"yes!\"   {{1}}   helping you feel close and   {{2}}   to people you care about, it turns out that hugs can bring a   {{3}}   of health benefits to your body and mind. Believe it or not, a warm embrace might even help you   {{4}}   getting sick this winter."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"In a recent study   {{5}}   over 400 healthy adults, researchers from Carnegie Mellon University in Pennsylvania examined the effects of perceived social support and the receipt of hugs   {{6}}   the participants' susceptibility to developing the common cold after being   {{7}}   to the virus. People who perceived greater social support were less likely to come   {{8}}   with a cold, and the researchers   {{9}}   that the stress-reducing effects of hugging   {{10}}   about 32 percent of that beneficial effect.   {{11}}   among those who got a cold, the ones who felt greater social support and received more frequent hugs had less severe   {{12}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"\"Hugging protects people who are under stress from the   {{13}}   risk for colds that's usually   {{14}}   with stress,\" notes Sheldon Cohen, a professor of psychology at Carnegie. Hugging \"is a marker of intimacy and helps   {{15}}   the feeling that others are there to help   {{16}}   difficulty.\""},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"Some experts   {{17}}   the stress-reducing, health-related benefits of hugging to the release of oxytocin, often called \"the bonding hormone\"   {{18}}   it promotes attachment in relationships, including that between mothers and their newborn babies. Oxytocin is made primarily in the central lower part of the brain, and some of it is released into the bloodstream. But some of it   {{19}}   in the brain, where it   {{20}}   mood, behavior and physiology."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Unlike"},{"key":"B","text":"Besides"},{"key":"C","text":"Despite"},{"key":"D","text":"Throughout"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"1.","reason":"前后两句都是拥抱的好处、并列叠加 线索在本句与上一句的并置：__(1)__ helping you feel close and __(2)__ to people you care about, it turns out that hugs can bring a __(3)__ of health benefits。前半句说拥抱让你与人亲近，主句说拥抱还带来健康好处——两者都是「拥抱的益处」，是叠加追加关系，答案应是「除……之外（还）」之意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Unlike意为「与……不同」，引出对比对象，但前后两部分都是拥抱的好处、并非对比，逻辑相反，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Besides意为「除……之外（还）」，正好把「让你亲近他人」这一好处与下文「带来健康好处」叠加起来，与前后同向追加的逻辑完全吻合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Despite意为「尽管」，引出让步——后半句应与前半句相反或意外。但「带来健康好处」并不与「让你亲近他人」相对立，逻辑指向错误。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Throughout意为「贯穿整个……」，后接时间或空间（如 throughout the year），接动名词短语既不搭配也无叠加逻辑，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"connected"},{"key":"B","text":"restricted"},{"key":"C","text":"equal"},{"key":"D","text":"inferior"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"与 close、care about 同向 线索在本句：helping you feel close and __(2)__ to people you care about。空与 close（亲近）由 and 并列、又指向 people you care about（你在乎的人），应是与「亲近」同向的褒义词——「与人相连」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"connected意为「与……相连的」，feel connected to people 即「感到与人相连」，与并列的 close 同向、又呼应 people you care about，语义最贴合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"restricted意为「受限制的」，feel restricted 是「感到受约束」，与 close 的亲近感方向相反，色彩冲突，故不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"equal意为「平等的」，强调地位对等，而非情感亲近，与 close 不构成同向并列，文意不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"inferior意为「低劣的、低人一等的」，是贬义，与表亲近的 close 方向相反，更不可能用来形容与所爱之人的关系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"choice"},{"key":"B","text":"view"},{"key":"C","text":"lesson"},{"key":"D","text":"host"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"3.","reason":"a host of＝大量 线索在本句框架：hugs can bring a __(3)__ of health benefits。a ___ of 后接复数 benefits，需要一个能表「许多、大量」的名词；a host of 是固定短语，意为「大量的」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"choice构成 a choice of 意为「……的选择余地」，但 benefits（好处）不是供人挑选的对象，文意不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"view构成 a view of 意为「……的景象/看法」，与 health benefits 搭配不当，无法表「大量好处」。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"lesson意为「课程、教训」，a lesson of 既非固定量词短语，也与 benefits 不搭，故不选。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"host构成固定短语 a host of，意为「大量的、许多的」，a host of health benefits＝「大量健康益处」，框架与文意（拥抱好处多）双双契合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"recall"},{"key":"B","text":"forget"},{"key":"C","text":"avoid"},{"key":"D","text":"keep"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"拥抱帮你不生病 线索在本句与全文基调：a warm embrace might even help you __(4)__ getting sick this winter。help you ___ getting sick，结合主旨「拥抱有益健康」，应是「帮你避免生病」，即避开这一负面结果。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"recall意为「回忆起」，help you recall getting sick＝「帮你回忆起生病」，与拥抱有益健康的主旨无关，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"forget意为「忘记」，help you forget getting sick 是「帮你忘记生病」，只是心理层面，并非真正阻止生病，与下文研究证明的「降低患感冒概率」不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"avoid意为「避免」，help you avoid getting sick＝「帮你避免生病」，既与 help 的正面方向一致，又精准对应后文研究「拥抱降低患感冒概率」的核心，最贴合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"keep意为「保持」，keep doing 是「持续做」，help you keep getting sick＝「帮你一直生病」，语义全反；若要表「使免于」须用 keep ... from doing，此处无 from，搭配也不成立。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"collecting"},{"key":"B","text":"involving"},{"key":"C","text":"guiding"},{"key":"D","text":"affecting"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"研究涉及400名成年人 线索在本句：In a recent study __(5)__ over 400 healthy adults, researchers ... examined the effects。study 与 over 400 healthy adults 之间是「研究涉及/包含这些受试者」的关系，应填表「涉及、包含」之意的词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"collecting意为「收集」，收集的应是数据、样本，而非「收集400名成年人」，与 adults 搭配不当。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"involving意为「涉及、（研究中）包含」，a study involving over 400 adults＝「一项涉及400多名成年人的研究」，是描述研究对象的地道搭配，最契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"guiding意为「引导、指导」，study guiding adults＝「指导成年人的研究」，研究与受试者之间不是指导关系，文意不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"affecting意为「影响」，study affecting adults＝「影响成年人的研究」，但此处要说研究以这些人为对象，而非研究去影响他们，语义偏离。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"of"},{"key":"B","text":"in"},{"key":"C","text":"at"},{"key":"D","text":"on"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"effect on＝对……的影响 线索在本句的中心名词 effects：examined the effects of perceived social support and the receipt of hugs __(6)__ the participants' susceptibility。表「对某事物的影响」固定用 effect on something，故空填 on。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"of在 the effects of ... 中已出现，of 引出施事（哪些因素的影响）；要表「对易感性的影响」须换用 on，再用 of 会逻辑重复、指向不清。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in表「在……之内」，effect in 不是表「对……的影响」的固定搭配，故不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"at表地点/时间点，effect at 不构成「对……的影响」之义，搭配错误。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"on与 effect 构成固定搭配 effect on，意为「对……的影响」，正好引出影响的对象 the participants' susceptibility，搭配与文意都对。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"devoted"},{"key":"B","text":"exposed"},{"key":"C","text":"lost"},{"key":"D","text":"attracted"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"感染前先接触病毒 线索在本句逻辑：susceptibility to developing the common cold after being __(7)__ to the virus。要研究「接触病毒后患感冒的易感性」，故 being ___ to the virus 应表「暴露于、接触到病毒」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"devoted构成 be devoted to 意为「致力于、献身于」，be devoted to the virus＝「献身于病毒」，文意荒谬，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"exposed构成固定搭配 be exposed to，意为「暴露于、接触到」，be exposed to the virus＝「接触到病毒」，正是患感冒的前提，搭配与逻辑双双契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"lost构成 be lost to 意为「失去、丧失给」，与「接触病毒」无关，逻辑不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"attracted构成 be attracted to 意为「被……吸引」，be attracted to the virus＝「被病毒吸引」，不合医学语境，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"across"},{"key":"B","text":"along"},{"key":"C","text":"down"},{"key":"D","text":"out"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"come down with＝患（病） 线索在本句语义：People who perceived greater social support were less likely to come __(8)__ with a cold。with a cold（得感冒）要求 come ___ 表「患病」，come down with 是固定短语，意为「患（病）」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"across构成 come across 意为「偶然遇到、碰见」，不与疾病搭配表「患病」，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"along构成 come along 意为「出现、进展、一起来」，与 with a cold 不构成「患病」之义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"down构成固定短语 come down with，意为「染上、患（病）」，come down with a cold＝「患感冒」，框架与语境（谁更不易感冒）完全吻合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"out构成 come out 意为「出来、出版、结果是」，不能与 with a cold 搭配表患病，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"calculated"},{"key":"B","text":"denied"},{"key":"C","text":"doubted"},{"key":"D","text":"imagined"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"得出32%这一量化结论 线索在 that 从句的内容：the researchers __(9)__ that the stress-reducing effects of hugging __(10)__ about 32 percent of that beneficial effect。从句给出精确数字 about 32 percent，研究者对数据应是「计算、测算」得出，故填 calculated。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"calculated意为「计算、测算」，与从句中 about 32 percent 这一量化结论严丝合缝——研究者通过数据计算出拥抱减压效应约占32%，最契合科研语境。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"denied意为「否认」，但全文在肯定拥抱的益处、该从句也在正面给出贡献比例，否认与上下文正向逻辑相悖，故不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"doubted意为「怀疑」，与研究者拿出确切数据的肯定态度矛盾，且本文基调是支持拥抱有益，故不选。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"imagined意为「想象、臆测」，但精确的32%是研究测算所得而非凭空想象，与科研严谨性冲突，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"served"},{"key":"B","text":"required"},{"key":"C","text":"restored"},{"key":"D","text":"explained"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"减压效应解释了32%的益处 线索在本句因果关系：the stress-reducing effects of hugging __(10)__ about 32 percent of that beneficial effect。拥抱的减压效应「占据/说明了」该有益效果的约32%，explain（用于统计指占某比例、可解释多少变异）正合此意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"served意为「服务、充当」，serve 32 percent of the effect 不构成「占某比例」之义，搭配不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"required意为「需要、要求」，「减压效应需要32%的益处」逻辑颠倒，与因果方向不符，故不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"restored意为「恢复、修复」，restore 32 percent of the effect＝「恢复了32%的效果」，此处并非「恢复」某已失去的效果，语义偏离。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"explained在统计语境意为「（某因素）可解释/占某比例的效应」，explained about 32 percent of that beneficial effect＝「解释了该益处约32%」，与研究测算的因果贡献完全契合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Even"},{"key":"B","text":"Still"},{"key":"C","text":"Rather"},{"key":"D","text":"Thus"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"进一步说连得病的人也获益 线索在前后两句的递进关系：上句说社会支持强者更不易感冒，本句__(11)__ among those who got a cold, the ones who felt greater social support ... had less severe __(12)__进一步说「即便在已得病者中」社会支持强者症状也更轻。这是「连……都」的递进强调，Even 最贴。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Even意为「甚至、连……都」，Even among those who got a cold＝「甚至在那些已感冒的人当中」，把好处推及最不利的子群，递进逻辑最贴合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Still意为「仍然、尽管如此」，多表轻微转折/让步，但本句与上句同向递进而非转折，且 Still 不能像 Even 那样修饰 among 短语表「甚至连」，不如 Even 贴切。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Rather意为「相反、而是」，用于否定前句、提出替代说法，但本句是补充递进而非纠正，逻辑不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Thus意为「因此」，表因果推论；但「连得病者也症状更轻」并非由上句直接推出的结果，而是另加的一层证据，因果关系不成立。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"defeats"},{"key":"B","text":"symptoms"},{"key":"C","text":"tests"},{"key":"D","text":"errors"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"已感冒者病情更轻＝症状更轻 线索在本句对象：among those who got a cold, the ones who felt greater social support ... had less severe __(12)__。说的是已感冒者，less severe ___ 指「更轻的（感冒）症状」，symptoms（症状）正与 a cold 对应。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"defeats意为「失败、挫败」，less severe defeats＝「不那么严重的失败」，与感冒病情无关，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"symptoms意为「症状」，less severe symptoms＝「更轻的症状」，正好描述已感冒者病情较轻，与 a cold 搭配自然，最契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"tests意为「测试、检查」，less severe tests 不通——感冒病情轻重无关「测试严重与否」，故不选。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"errors意为「错误」，less severe errors＝「不那么严重的错误」，与感冒症状无关，文意不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"minimized"},{"key":"B","text":"highlighted"},{"key":"C","text":"controlled"},{"key":"D","text":"increased"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"压力本会增大患感冒风险 线索在本句逻辑与下一空呼应：Hugging protects people who are under stress from the __(13)__ risk for colds that's usually __(14)__ with stress。拥抱保护人「免受」压力带来的风险，可见这风险是被压力「升高」的；下文 usually associated with stress 也印证压力会抬高风险，故填 increased。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"minimized意为「使最小化、降到最低」，「降到最低的风险」无须 protect from，与「拥抱保护人免受风险」逻辑相反，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"highlighted意为「突出、强调」，highlighted risk＝「被强调的风险」，指认知层面被凸显，并非压力实际抬高了风险，与医学因果不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"controlled意为「被控制的」，controlled risk＝「受控的风险」，风险既已受控就无须拥抱来防护，与上下文方向相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"increased意为「增大的、升高的」，the increased risk for colds＝「（因压力）升高的感冒风险」，正是拥抱要帮人抵御的对象，逻辑与下文 associated with stress 完全吻合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"equipped"},{"key":"B","text":"associated"},{"key":"C","text":"presented"},{"key":"D","text":"compared"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"14.","reason":"风险与压力相关联 线索在本句：the __(13)__ risk for colds that's usually __(14)__ with stress。要表「（这风险）通常与压力相关联」，be associated with 是固定搭配，意为「与……相关」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"equipped构成 be equipped with 意为「配备有」，「风险配备压力」文意不通，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"associated构成固定搭配 be associated with，意为「与……相关联」，risk associated with stress＝「与压力相关的风险」，搭配与文意双双契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"presented构成 present ... with 意为「向某人呈交/赠予」，与「风险和压力相关」之义不符，故不选。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"compared构成 be compared with 意为「与……相比」，但此处不是把风险和压力作比较，而是说二者相关，逻辑不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"assess"},{"key":"B","text":"moderate"},{"key":"C","text":"generate"},{"key":"D","text":"record"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"拥抱产生被支持的感受 线索在本句与主旨：Hugging \"is a marker of intimacy and helps __(15)__ the feeling that others are there to help __(16)__ difficulty.\"。拥抱是亲密的标志，帮助「产生/营造」别人会在困难时相助的感受，generate（产生）正合此意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"assess意为「评估、评价」，「拥抱帮助评估某种感受」逻辑不通——拥抱是带来感受而非评判它，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"moderate意为「使缓和、减轻」，moderate the feeling 是「削弱这种感受」，但这是正面感受（有人相助），削弱它与主旨相反，故不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"generate意为「产生、生成」，generate the feeling that others are there to help＝「营造出别人会在困境中相助的感受」，与拥抱的正面作用、亲密标志完全契合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"record意为「记录」，「拥抱帮助记录某种感受」不合逻辑——感受是被拥抱激发的，而非被记录，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in the face of"},{"key":"B","text":"in the form of"},{"key":"C","text":"in the way of"},{"key":"D","text":"in the name of"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"16.","reason":"面对困难时有人相助 线索在本句语义：others are there to help __(16)__ difficulty。意为「在面对困难时别人会来帮忙」，in the face of difficulty 是固定短语，意为「面对困难」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"in the face of意为「面对、面临」，help in the face of difficulty＝「在面对困难时给予帮助」，与「别人会在你遇到困难时相助」的语境完全契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in the form of意为「以……的形式」，help in the form of difficulty＝「以困难的形式帮助」，文意荒谬，故不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"in the way of意为「妨碍」或「在……方面」，均不能表「面对困难给予帮助」，与正面相助的语境不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"in the name of意为「以……的名义」，help in the name of difficulty＝「以困难的名义帮助」，逻辑不通，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"transfer"},{"key":"B","text":"commit"},{"key":"C","text":"attribute"},{"key":"D","text":"return"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"17.","reason":"把益处归因于催产素释放 线索在本句因果：Some experts __(17)__ the stress-reducing, health-related benefits of hugging to the release of oxytocin。专家把拥抱的益处「归因于」催产素的释放，attribute A to B 是固定搭配，意为「把 A 归因于 B」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"transfer构成 transfer A to B 意为「把 A 转移到 B」，但益处不是被「转移」到催产素，而是被归因于它，语义不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"commit构成 commit ... to 意为「把……交托/致力于」，不表「归因」，与 the benefits ... to the release 的因果关系不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"attribute构成固定搭配 attribute A to B，意为「把 A 归因于 B」，attribute the benefits to the release of oxytocin＝「把这些益处归因于催产素的释放」，搭配与因果逻辑完全契合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"return构成 return A to B 意为「把 A 归还给 B」，与「把益处归因于催产素」之义不符，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"because"},{"key":"B","text":"unless"},{"key":"C","text":"though"},{"key":"D","text":"until"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"18.","reason":"之所以叫结合激素，因它促进依恋 线索在前后两部分的因果：often called \"the bonding hormone\" __(18)__ it promotes attachment in relationships。催产素被称为「结合激素」，是「因为」它促进关系中的依恋——后半句是前半句称呼的原因，故填 because。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"because意为「因为」，引出催产素被称作「结合激素」的原因——它促进关系中的依恋，因果逻辑严丝合缝，最契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"unless意为「除非」，表否定条件，「除非它促进依恋」与「被称为结合激素」之间无条件关系，逻辑不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"though意为「尽管」，表让步转折，但「促进依恋」恰是叫它结合激素的理由，并非相反，方向错误，故不选。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"until意为「直到」，表时间界限，与「称呼—原因」的因果关系无关，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"emerges"},{"key":"B","text":"vanishes"},{"key":"C","text":"remains"},{"key":"D","text":"decreases"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"与『释放入血』相对，部分留在脑中 线索在 But 引导的对比：some of it is released into the bloodstream. But some of it __(19)__ in the brain, where it __(20)__ mood。前句说一部分进入血液，But 转折说另一部分「留在」脑中（并在那里作用于情绪），remains（保留、留存）正与「被释放出去」相对。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"emerges意为「出现、浮现」，但催产素本就产于脑中，不是「在脑中出现」，且与前句「释放入血」的对比关系不成立，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"vanishes意为「消失」，但后半句 where it influences mood 说明这部分仍在脑中发挥作用，若已「消失」则无从作用，前后矛盾。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"remains意为「保留、留存」，some of it remains in the brain＝「一部分留在脑中」，与前句「释放入血」形成对比，又与后文「在脑中影响情绪」衔接，最契合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"decreases意为「减少」，「一部分在脑中减少」既与对比逻辑不符，也无法引出 where it influences mood，故不选。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"experiences"},{"key":"B","text":"combines"},{"key":"C","text":"justifies"},{"key":"D","text":"influences"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"催产素在脑中作用于情绪等 线索在本句：some of it __(19)__ in the brain, where it __(20)__ mood, behavior and physiology。留在脑中的催产素对情绪、行为和生理产生「作用、影响」，influences（影响）正合此意，也呼应全文「催产素带来身心益处」的主线。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"experiences意为「经历、体验」，体验情绪的应是人，而非催产素这种物质，主体错位，故不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"combines意为「结合、合并」，「催产素结合情绪、行为、生理」语义不通，且 combine 多与 with 连用，搭配也不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"justifies意为「证明……有理、为……辩护」，「催产素为情绪辩护」逻辑荒谬，与机制说明不符，故不选。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"influences意为「影响」，it influences mood, behavior and physiology＝「它影响情绪、行为和生理」，正是催产素在脑中的作用，与全文「催产素带来身心好处」主线完全契合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"First two hours, now three hours – this is how far in advance authorities are recommending people show up to catch a domestic flight, at least at some major U.S. airports with increasingly massive security lines."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Americans are willing to tolerate time-consuming security procedures in return for increased safety. The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804, which terrorists may have downed over the Mediterranean Sea, provides another tragic reminder of why. But demanding too much of air travelers or providing too little security in return undermines public support for the process. And it should: Wasted time is a drag on Americans' economic and private lives, not to mention infuriating."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"Last year, the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) found in a secret check that undercover investigators were able to sneak weapons – both fake and real – past airport security nearly every time they tried. Enhanced security measures since then, combined with a rise in airline travel due to the improving economy and low oil prices, have resulted in long waits at major airports such as Chicago's O'Hare International. It is not yet clear how much more effective airline security has become – but the lines are obvious."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Part of the issue is that the government did not anticipate the steep increase in airline travel, so the TSA is now rushing to get new screeners on the line. Part of the issue is that airports have only so much room for screening lanes. Another factor may be that more people are trying to overpack their carry-on bags to avoid checked-baggage fees, though the airlines strongly dispute this."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"There is one step the TSA could take that would not require remodeling airports or rushing to hire: Enroll more people in the PreCheck program. PreCheck is supposed to be a win-win for travelers and the TSA. Passengers who pass a background check are eligible to use expedited screening lanes. This allows the TSA to focus on travelers who are higher risk, saving time for everyone involved. The TSA wants to enroll 25 million people in PreCheck."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"It has not gotten anywhere close to that, and one big reason is sticker shock: Passengers must pay $85 every five years to process their background checks. Since the beginning, this price tag has been PreCheck's fatal flaw. Upcoming reforms might bring the price to a more reasonable level. But Congress should look into doing so directly, by helping to finance PreCheck enrollment or to cut costs in other ways."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-7","text":"The TSA cannot continue diverting resources into underused PreCheck lanes while most of the traveling public suffers in unnecessary lines. It is long past time to make the program work."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804 is mentioned to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"explain American's tolerance of current security checks."},{"key":"B","text":"stress the urgency to strengthen security worldwide."},{"key":"C","text":"highlight the necessity of upgrading major U.S. airports."},{"key":"D","text":"emphasize the importance of privacy protection."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"提到埃及航空804号航班坠毁是为了____","choicesZh":{"A":"解释美国人对当前安检措施的容忍","B":"强调在全球范围内加强安全措施的紧迫性","C":"突出美国主要机场升级改造的必要性","D":"强调隐私保护的重要性"},"analysis":{"type":"The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804 is mentioned to这种\"X is mentioned to + 动词\"结构，问的是举例的目的而非例子本身的内容。","parse":"The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804 is mentioned to是一个被动语态的不完整句，主语是事件名，谓语\"is mentioned to\"后接动词原形，四个选项各自补全这个不定式，问举例目的，结构无陷阱。","locateEn":"Americans are willing to tolerate time-consuming security procedures in return for increased safety. The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804, which terrorists may have downed over the Mediterranean Sea, provides another tragic reminder of why.","locateZh":"美国人愿意忍受耗时的安检程序以换取更高的安全；埃及航空804号航班坠毁（可能是恐怖分子在地中海上空将其击落）又一次悲剧性地提醒了人们\"为什么愿意忍受\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"由预判\"为何愿意忍受\"出发，A选项explain American's tolerance of current security checks.精确对应——例子的功能就是\"解释容忍\"。","pairs":[{"orig":"Americans are willing to tolerate time-consuming security procedures in return for increased safety.","opt":"explain American's tolerance of current security checks."},{"orig":"provides another tragic reminder of why","opt":"explain"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只谈美国国内航空安检（domestic flight/Americans），未涉及\"worldwide\"全球范围。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文升级机场的讨论在后文（第5-7段是关于PreCheck），与EgyptAir这例子无关；例子的作用不是论证\"升级机场\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未提及\"隐私保护\"，privacy一词在全文不曾出现，纯属杜撰。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"Which of the following contributes to long waits at major airports?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"New restrictions on carry-on bags."},{"key":"B","text":"The declining efficiency of the TSA."},{"key":"C","text":"An increase in the number of travelers."},{"key":"D","text":"Frequent unexpected secret checks."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"以下哪项导致了主要机场的长时间等待?","choicesZh":{"A":"对随身行李的新限制","B":"TSA效率的下降","C":"旅客数量的增加","D":"频繁的突击秘密检查"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following contributes to long waits at major airports?问的是哪一项客观因素属于原文给出的原因，需要在原文中找具体对应。","parse":"Which of the following contributes to long waits at major airports?主干是Which contributes to long waits，contribute to为\"导致/促成\"，介词宾语是long waits，整体平铺直叙无陷阱。","locateEn":"Part of the issue is that the government did not anticipate the steep increase in airline travel, so the TSA is now rushing to get new screeners on the line. Part of the issue is that airports have only so much room for screening lanes. Another factor may be that more people are trying to overpack their carry-on bags to avoid checked-baggage fees, though the airlines strongly dispute this.","locateZh":"部分原因是政府未预见到航空出行的陡增，TSA现在正赶着招新的安检员；部分原因是机场可用于安检通道的空间有限；另一个因素可能是更多人为了避免托运行李费而过度打包随身行李——尽管航空公司对此强烈反驳。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是\"乘客过度打包随身行李\"为现状（且航空公司有异议），从未提到\"对随身行李的新限制\"——A是把原文话题反转表述。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文未指责TSA效率下降；相反，第4段说TSA在\"加紧招人\"，第3段提到加强安检措施，但都没有\"效率下降\"的判断。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"由预判\"出行人数激增\"出发，CAn increase in the number of travelers.与原文两处描述完全等值，是唯一命中枚举原因的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"the government did not anticipate the steep increase in airline travel","opt":"An increase in the number of travelers."},{"orig":"a rise in airline travel due to the improving economy and low oil prices","opt":"An increase in the number of travelers."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文只提到去年TSA一次的\"secret check\"（a secret check），且这次检查是揭示安检漏洞，并不是\"频繁\"也不是导致长队的原因。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The word \"expedited\" (Line 4, Para. 5) is closest in meaning to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"quieter."},{"key":"B","text":"cheaper."},{"key":"C","text":"wider."},{"key":"D","text":"faster."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"单词\"expedited\"(第5段第4行)在意思上最接近____","choicesZh":{"A":"更安静的","B":"更便宜的","C":"更宽的","D":"更快的"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"expedited\" (Line 4, Para. 5) is closest in meaning to明确问某词在文中的意思，最近似哪一项。","parse":"The word \"expedited\" (Line 4, Para. 5) is closest in meaning to是常规词义题问法，被问词以引号标出，无歧义。","locateEn":"Passengers who pass a background check are eligible to use expedited screening lanes. This allows the TSA to focus on travelers who are higher risk, saving time for everyone involved.","locateZh":"通过背景审查的旅客有资格使用\"快速安检通道\"。这让TSA可以专注于高风险旅客，为所有相关者节省时间。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文未提及噪音问题，quieter纯属无关。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"PreCheck的代价是后文Passengers must pay $85——它本身是要花钱的，cheaper反而与原文相悖；且expedited一词本身不涉及价格。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文无任何\"通道更宽\"的表述，wider属臆造。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"由预判\"快速/省时\"出发，Dfaster.最贴合\"saving time\"这一上下文线索。","pairs":[{"orig":"saving time for everyone involved","opt":"faster."},{"orig":"expedited screening lanes","opt":"faster."}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"One problem with the PreCheck program is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a dramatic reduction of its scale."},{"key":"B","text":"its wrongly-directed implementation."},{"key":"C","text":"the government's reluctance to back it."},{"key":"D","text":"an unreasonable price for enrollment."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"PreCheck项目的一个问题是____","choicesZh":{"A":"其规模大幅缩减","B":"其实施方向错误","C":"政府不愿意支持该项目","D":"注册费用不合理"},"analysis":{"type":"One problem with the PreCheck program is要求把原文中描述的那个问题用一个选项概括出来，属于具体信息细节比对题。","parse":"One problem with the PreCheck program is主干\"One problem ... is____\"，with the PreCheck program作problem的修饰，结构简单。","locateEn":"It has not gotten anywhere close to that, and one big reason is sticker shock: Passengers must pay $85 every five years to process their background checks. Since the beginning, this price tag has been PreCheck's fatal flaw.","locateZh":"它（入选人数）远未接近那个目标，一个大原因是\"价签冲击\"：旅客每5年必须支付85美元来处理背景审查；从一开始，这个价格就一直是PreCheck的致命缺陷。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文说TSAwants to enroll 25 million people、目标扩大；从未减少规模，A方向相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未说PreCheck实施方向\"错\"，只说收费高导致入选不足——B的\"方向错位\"是杜撰。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文末句呼吁Congress should look into doing so directly, by helping to finance PreCheck enrollment——国会被建议出手支持，并非\"不愿支持\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"由预判\"收费过高\"出发，Dan unreasonable price for enrollment.精确锁定原文对价格的负面评价。","pairs":[{"orig":"Passengers must pay $85 every five years to process their background checks.","opt":"an unreasonable price for enrollment."},{"orig":"this price tag has been PreCheck's fatal flaw","opt":"an unreasonable price for enrollment."}]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Less Screening for More Safety"},{"key":"B","text":"PreCheck – a Belated Solution"},{"key":"C","text":"Getting Stuck in Security Lines"},{"key":"D","text":"Underused PreCheck Lanes"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项是本文的最佳标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"更少的安检带来更多的安全","B":"PreCheck——一个姗姗来迟的解决方案","C":"困在安检队伍中","D":"未被充分利用的PreCheck通道"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?问全文最佳标题，需要覆盖全文而非某段。","parse":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?虚拟语气would be表\"会是\"，句式无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未主张\"少安检换安全\"——相反它认可加强安检（Enhanced security measures）的必要，只是希望通过PreCheck分流来兼顾。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"PreCheck只是第5-6段提出的一条对策，且原文并未称它是\"姗姗来迟的解法\"——它一开始就存在，问题是收费太高导致入选不足；以PreCheck作标题只覆盖一部分。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"由全文主线\"长队\"出发，CGetting Stuck in Security Lines是唯一同时覆盖现象（首段）、成因（第3-4段）、对策困境（5-6段）和呼吁（末段）的标题。","pairs":[{"orig":"three hours – this is how far in advance authorities are recommending people show up to catch a domestic flight, at least at some major U.S. airports with increasingly massive security lines.","opt":"Getting Stuck in Security Lines"},{"orig":"most of the traveling public suffers in unnecessary lines","opt":"Getting Stuck in Security Lines"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Underused PreCheck Lanes（被闲置的PreCheck通道）仅是末段underused PreCheck lanes的一个细节描述，无法覆盖全文谈\"长队-原因-解药-呼吁\"的整体主线。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"\"The ancient Hawaiians were astronomers,\" wrote Queen Liliuokalani, Hawaii's last reigning monarch, in 1897. Star watchers were among the most esteemed members of Hawaiian society. Sadly, all is not well with astronomy in Hawaii today. Protests have erupted over construction of the Thirty Meter Telescope (TMT), a giant observatory that promises to revolutionize humanity's view of the cosmos."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"At issue is the TMT's planned location on Mauna Kea, a dormant volcano worshiped by some Hawaiians as the piko, that connects the Hawaiian Islands to the heavens. But Mauna Kea is also home to some of the world's most powerful telescopes. Resting in the Pacific Ocean, Mauna Kea's peak rises above the bulk of our planet's dense atmosphere, where conditions allow telescopes to obtain images of unsurpassed clarity."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Opposition to telescopes on Mauna Kea is nothing new. A small but vocal group of Hawaiians and environmentalists have long viewed their presence as disrespect for sacred land and a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Some blame for the current controversy belongs to astronomers. In their eagerness to build bigger telescopes, they forgot that science is not the only way of understanding the world. They did not always prioritize the protection of Mauna Kea's fragile ecosystems or its holiness to the island's inhabitants. Hawaiian culture is not a relic of the past; it is a living culture undergoing a renaissance today."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"Yet science has a cultural history, too, with roots going back to the dawn of civilization. The same curiosity to find what lies beyond the horizon that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii's shores inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens. Calls to disassemble all telescopes on Mauna Kea or to ban future development there ignore the reality that astronomy and Hawaiian culture both seek to answer big questions about who we are, where we come from and where we are going. Perhaps that is why we explore the starry skies, as if answering a primal calling to know ourselves and our true ancestral homes."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"The astronomy community is making compromises to change its use of Mauna Kea. The TMT site was chosen to minimize the telescope's visibility around the island and to avoid archaeological and environmental impact. To limit the number of telescopes on Mauna Kea, old ones will be removed at the end of their lifetimes and their sites returned to a natural state. There is no reason why everyone cannot be welcomed on Mauna Kea to embrace their cultural heritage and to study the stars."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"Queen Liliuokalani's remark in Paragraph 1 indicates____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"her conservative view on the historical role of astronomy."},{"key":"B","text":"the importance of astronomy in ancient Hawaiian society."},{"key":"C","text":"the regrettable decline of astronomy in ancient times."},{"key":"D","text":"her appreciation of star watchers' feats in her time."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第一段中Liliuokalani女王的话表明____","choicesZh":{"A":"她对天文学历史作用持保守看法","B":"天文学在古代夏威夷社会中的重要性","C":"天文学在古代令人遗憾的衰落","D":"她对其时代观星者功绩的赞赏"},"analysis":{"type":"indicates 要求把 Queen Liliuokalani 那句话的客观含义说清楚，而非延伸推断，属于细节理解。","parse":"Queen Liliuokalani's remark in Paragraph 1 indicates 是一个待补全的主谓结构：主语 Queen Liliuokalani's remark，谓语 indicates 后接选项作宾语。句式平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"\"The ancient Hawaiians were astronomers,\" wrote Queen Liliuokalani, Hawaii's last reigning monarch, in 1897. Star watchers were among the most esteemed members of Hawaiian society.","locateZh":"\"古代夏威夷人是天文学家，\"夏威夷最后一位在位君主 Liliuokalani 女王在 1897 年这样写道。观星者属于夏威夷社会中最受尊崇的成员之列。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文女王只是赞美古夏威夷人是天文学家，没有任何评价她个人对天文学历史角色\"保守与否\"的信息。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判结论\"古夏威夷社会高度重视天文\"和 the importance of astronomy in ancient Hawaiian society. 在主语、谓语、范围上一一对应，无多余成分，是定位句的标准同义改写。","pairs":[{"orig":"Star watchers were among the most esteemed members of Hawaiian society.","opt":"the importance of astronomy in ancient Hawaiian society."},{"orig":"The ancient Hawaiians","opt":"ancient Hawaiian society"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文将\"衰落\"明确放在今天——Sadly, all is not well with astronomy in Hawaii today.；选项却把衰落安到 in ancient times 古代，把时间从\"今天\"偷换成\"古代\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"in her time 把对象限定到女王自己的时代，而原文女王引用的是 The ancient Hawaiians 古代夏威夷人；同时她并未表达对\"她那个时代\"观星者的 appreciation。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"Mauna Kea is deemed as an ideal astronomical site due to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"its geographical features."},{"key":"B","text":"its protective surroundings."},{"key":"C","text":"its religious implications."},{"key":"D","text":"its existing infrastructure."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Mauna Kea被视为理想的天文观测地点是由于____","choicesZh":{"A":"其地理特征","B":"其防护性周边环境","C":"其宗教意涵","D":"其现有的基础设施"},"analysis":{"type":"due to 要求从原文找出 Mauna Kea 被视为理想台址的客观原因，是原文已写明的事实。","parse":"Mauna Kea is deemed as an ideal astronomical site due to____ 是 \"被动 + due to\" 结构。is deemed as = 被认为是；due to 引出原因，后接选项作介宾。无生僻结构。","locateEn":"Resting in the Pacific Ocean, Mauna Kea's peak rises above the bulk of our planet's dense atmosphere, where conditions allow telescopes to obtain images of unsurpassed clarity.","locateZh":"Mauna Kea 坐落于太平洋之中，其山顶高出地球大部分稠密大气层之上，那里的环境条件使望远镜能够获得无与伦比的清晰图像。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"山高超出稠密大气、成像清晰\"全部落在\"地理\"维度，its geographical features. 恰好以一个上位词概括，无超额、无遗漏。","pairs":[{"orig":"Resting in the Pacific Ocean, Mauna Kea's peak rises above the bulk of our planet's dense atmosphere","opt":"its geographical features."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是\"高出大气层\"，从未提到 Mauna Kea 周边有什么 protective surroundings. 保护性环境；这一概念在原文找不到任何对应。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"its religious implications. 对应的是 a dormant volcano worshiped by some Hawaiians as the piko, that connects the Hawaiian Islands to the heavens.——这是 Mauna Kea 的宗教意义，与\"为何是理想天文台址\"完全是两条线，回答的不是 Q27 问的问题。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文是说\"因为条件好，所以放了世界上最强大的望远镜\"——望远镜是\"好台址\"的结果；选项却把\"已有的基础设施 its existing infrastructure.\" 反过来当成它成为理想台址的原因。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"The construction of the TMT is opposed by some locals partly because____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"it may risk ruining their intellectual life."},{"key":"B","text":"it reminds them of a humiliating history."},{"key":"C","text":"their culture will lose a chance of revival."},{"key":"D","text":"they fear losing control of Mauna Kea."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"TMT的建设遭到一些当地人反对,部分原因是____","choicesZh":{"A":"它可能有损害他们精神生活的风险","B":"它使他们想起一段屈辱的历史","C":"他们的文化将失去复兴的机会","D":"他们担心失去对Mauna Kea的控制"},"analysis":{"type":"partly because 要求从原文找出反对者给出的某一条具体理由，原文必有明文支持。","parse":"The construction of the TMT is opposed by some locals partly because____ 是被动句 + 原因状语从句。主干 The construction ... is opposed by some locals，partly because 引出选项作原因从句。结构清晰。","locateEn":"A small but vocal group of Hawaiians and environmentalists have long viewed their presence as disrespect for sacred land and a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation.","locateZh":"一小批但很有声量的夏威夷人与环保人士长期以来都把这些望远镜的存在视为对圣地的不敬，并且是一种令人痛苦的提醒：提醒人们这片土地曾经是一个被吞并的主权国家。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是对圣地的不敬与历史伤痛，从未提到 intellectual life 智识生活会被毁；这一概念毫无原文对应。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"\"屈辱历史的痛苦提醒\"与 it reminds them of a humiliating history. 三要素（主语 it=TMT 在地存在、谓语 remind、对象 humiliating history）一一对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation.","opt":"it reminds them of a humiliating history."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P4 原文是 Hawaiian culture is not a relic of the past; it is a living culture undergoing a renaissance today.，明确说夏威夷文化\"正在复兴\"，选项却反过来说将\"失去复兴机会\"，方向恰好相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说望远镜的存在令人想起被吞并的过去，并没有说当地人\"害怕失去对 Mauna Kea 的控制权\"；fear losing control 在原文找不到任何对应。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 that progress in today's astronomy____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is fulfilling the dreams of ancient Hawaiians."},{"key":"B","text":"helps spread Hawaiian culture across the world."},{"key":"C","text":"may uncover the origin of Hawaiian culture."},{"key":"D","text":"will eventually soften Hawaiians' hostility."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第五段可以推断出当今天文学的进步____","choicesZh":{"A":"正在实现古代夏威夷人的梦想","B":"有助于向全世界传播夏威夷文化","C":"可能揭示夏威夷文化的起源","D":"最终将缓和夏威夷人的敌意"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 明确要求推断，答案在原文不会有原句，只能由定位句做\"一步\"延伸。","parse":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 that progress in today's astronomy____ 是 \"It + 被动 + that 从句\" 形式主语句。it 形式主语，真正主语是 that 从句；从句主语是 progress in today's astronomy，谓语接选项。结构常见、无陷阱。","locateEn":"The same curiosity to find what lies beyond the horizon that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii's shores inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens.","locateZh":"当年驱使早期波利尼西亚人来到夏威夷海岸、想看看地平线外有什么的那同一种好奇心，如今也激励着天文学家去探索星空。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"从\"两代探索者动机同源\"到\"今天的天文进步是在实现古夏威夷人的探索梦想\"只走一步推论；选项 A 既未超出 P5 范围，也没引入 P6 的妥协议程，是干净的一步延伸。","pairs":[{"orig":"The same curiosity to find what lies beyond the horizon that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii's shores inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens.","opt":"is fulfilling the dreams of ancient Hawaiians."},{"orig":"astronomers today to explore the heavens","opt":"is fulfilling the dreams"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"P5 全段从未谈天文学进步对夏威夷文化的对外\"传播\"作用，spread Hawaiian culture across the world 在原文完全无据。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文说天文与夏威夷文化都\"追问 who/where 这类大问题\"，但并没有说天文学的进步将\"揭示夏威夷文化的起源\"；从\"共同提问\"跨到\"揭示起源\"是越界推断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"\"软化敌意\"对应的是 P6 妥协措施可能带来的结果，但题干 Paragraph 5 明确要求只看 P5；且原文从未说\"天文进步\"本身会软化夏威夷人的敌意。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"The author's attitude toward choosing Mauna Kea as the TMT site is one of____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"severe criticism."},{"key":"B","text":"passive acceptance."},{"key":"C","text":"slight hesitancy."},{"key":"D","text":"full approval."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对选择Mauna Kea作为TMT选址的态度是____","choicesZh":{"A":"严厉批评","B":"被动接受","C":"略有犹豫","D":"完全赞成"},"analysis":{"type":"attitude 是态度题的标准信号词，答案是表态极性词（赞成/反对/中立/担忧等）。","parse":"The author's attitude toward choosing Mauna Kea as the TMT site is one of____：主语 The author's attitude，介词短语 toward choosing Mauna Kea as the TMT site 是定语修饰 attitude，系表结构 is one of____ 接选项作表语。注意 toward 后的动名词 choosing 不是真正的谓语。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"作者全文没有任何\"严厉批评\"选址的句子；P4 的批评对象是\"科学家此前的态度\"而非\"选址行为\"，severe criticism. 在评价对象和情感强度上都错。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"\"被动接受\"暗含\"心里不情愿、形势所迫\"；但 P6 用 There is no reason why everyone cannot be welcomed 是主动、热烈的认可，与 passive acceptance. 的被动感矛盾。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"\"略带犹豫\"要求文中有保留性副词或转折让步；P6 末句是无保留的双重否定，没有任何 slight hesitancy. 的标记。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"P5 否定极端反对 + P6 双重否定肯定共存——两处都把极性推到\"支持\"且无保留，因此 full approval. 中的 full（完全）正好对位。","pairs":[{"orig":"There is no reason why everyone cannot be welcomed on Mauna Kea to embrace their cultural heritage and to study the stars.","opt":"full approval."},{"orig":"Calls to disassemble all telescopes on Mauna Kea or to ban future development there ignore the reality","opt":"full approval."}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"Robert F. Kennedy once said that a country's GDP measures \"everything except that which makes life worthwhile.\" With Britain voting to leave the European Union, and GDP already predicted to slow as a result, it is now a timely moment to assess what he was referring to."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"The question of GDP and its usefulness has annoyed policymakers for over half a century. Many argue that it is a flawed concept. It measures things that do not matter and misses things that do. By most recent measures, the UK's GDP has been the envy of the Western world, with record low unemployment and high growth figures. If everything was going so well, then why did over 17 million people vote for Brexit, despite the warnings about what it could do to their country's economic prospects?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"A recent annual study of countries and their ability to convert growth into well-being sheds some light on that question. Across the 163 countries measured, the UK is one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements for its citizens. Rather than just focusing on GDP, over 40 different sets of criteria from health, education and civil society engagement have been measured to get a more rounded assessment of how countries are performing."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"While all of these countries face their own challenges, there are a number of consistent themes. Yes, there has been a budding economic recovery since the 2008 global crash, but in key indicators in areas such as health and education, major economies have continued to decline. Yet this isn't the case with all countries. Some relatively poor European countries have seen huge improvements across measures including civil society, income equality and the environment."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"This is a lesson that rich countries can learn: When GDP is no longer regarded as the sole measure of a country's success, the world looks very different."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"So, what Kennedy was referring to was that while GDP has been the most common method for measuring the economic activity of nations, as a measure, it is no longer enough. It does not include important factors such as environmental quality or education outcomes – all things that contribute to a person's sense of well-being."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-7","text":"The sharp hit to growth predicted around the world and in the UK could lead to a decline in the everyday services we depend on for our well-being and for growth. But policymakers who refocus efforts on improving well-being rather than simply worrying about GDP figures could avoid the forecasted doom and may even see progress."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"Robert F. Kennedy is cited because he____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"praised the UK for its GDP."},{"key":"B","text":"identified GDP with happiness."},{"key":"C","text":"misinterpreted the role of GDP."},{"key":"D","text":"had a low opinion of GDP."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"引用Robert F. Kennedy是因为他____","choicesZh":{"A":"称赞英国的GDP。","B":"将GDP等同于幸福。","C":"误解了GDP的作用。","D":"对GDP评价不高。"},"analysis":{"type":"cited because he____ 表面问 Kennedy 被引用的原因,实则要从他那句话+作者对它的态度推断他对 GDP 的看法,属于隐性推断题。","parse":"Robert F. Kennedy is cited because he____ 是简单的因果状语从句结构,主句被动 (is cited),because 引出原因。空格补的是 he 后面的谓语,所以四个选项都是动词短语,无陷阱。","locateEn":"Robert F. Kennedy once said that a country's GDP measures \"everything except that which makes life worthwhile.\"","locateZh":"罗伯特·F·肯尼迪曾说,一国的 GDP 衡量了 \"除了那些让生活值得过的东西以外的一切\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P1 Kennedy 的话泛指 a country's GDP,并未涉及英国,更没有 praised the UK for its GDP 这种赞扬。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"everything except that which makes life worthwhile 恰恰说 GDP 与 \"让生活有意义的事\" 是排除关系,选项却说 identified GDP with happiness(把 GDP 等同于幸福),与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Kennedy 是对 GDP 提出限度上的批评,作者也支持他;并没有说他 misinterpreted the role of GDP(误解了 GDP 的角色)。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是 \"看不起 GDP\";四项中只有 had a low opinion of GDP 直接表达低评价,锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"everything except that which makes life worthwhile","opt":"had a low opinion of GDP"}]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the UK is reluctant to remold its economic pattern."},{"key":"B","text":"GDP as the measure of success is widely defied in the UK."},{"key":"C","text":"the UK will contribute less to the world economy."},{"key":"D","text":"policymakers in the UK are paying less attention to GDP."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第2段可以推断出____","choicesZh":{"A":"英国不愿意重塑其经济模式。","B":"将GDP作为成功衡量标准在英国受到广泛质疑。","C":"英国对世界经济的贡献将会减少。","D":"英国的政策制定者对GDP的关注度正在下降。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that____ 中的 inferred 直接判定为推断题。","parse":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that____ 中 It 是形式主语,真正主语是 that 引导的从句(也就是四个选项要补的内容);from Paragraph 2 是状语,限定证据来源。结构常见,无理解陷阱。","locateEn":"Many argue that it is a flawed concept. It measures things that do not matter and misses things that do. By most recent measures, the UK's GDP has been the envy of the Western world, with record low unemployment and high growth figures. If everything was going so well, then why did over 17 million people vote for Brexit, despite the warnings about what it could do to their country's economic prospects?","locateZh":"许多人认为 GDP 是有缺陷的概念,它度量了不重要的东西、却漏掉了重要的东西。按最新数据,英国的 GDP 一直是西方世界羡慕的对象——失业率创新低、增速亮眼。但若一切如此美好,为什么会有超过 1700 万人不顾对国家经济前景的警告而投票脱欧?","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"第二段只展示了 GDP 数据与民意的反差,没有任何关于 reluctant to remold its economic pattern(不愿重塑经济模式)的表述。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"GDP as the measure of success is widely defied in the UK 把反问的隐含否定显化为陈述,与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"If everything was going so well, then why did over 17 million people vote for Brexit, despite the warnings about what it could do to their country's economic prospects?","opt":"GDP as the measure of success is widely defied in the UK"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"段落只在英国国内 GDP 与民意之间做对比,没有 contribute less to the world economy(对世界经济贡献减少)这一全球维度。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"段落里反对 GDP 的是 over 17 million people(选民),而非 policymakers in the UK(决策者);把质疑主体偷换为政策制定者,与原文不符。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"Which of the following is true about the recent annual study?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is sponsored by 163 countries."},{"key":"B","text":"It excludes GDP as an indicator."},{"key":"C","text":"Its criteria are questionable."},{"key":"D","text":"Its results are enlightening."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于最近的年度研究,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"它由163个国家资助。","B":"它排除了GDP作为指标。","C":"它的标准值得商榷。","D":"它的结果具有启发性。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true about the recent annual study? 问的是该研究自身的属性,答案必须能在介绍这项研究的句子里直接核对。","parse":"Which of the following is true about the recent annual study? 是 Which 引导的特殊疑问句,about 介词短语限定核对对象。四个选项均为独立陈述句,直接与定位句比对即可。","locateEn":"A recent annual study of countries and their ability to convert growth into well-being sheds some light on that question. Across the 163 countries measured, the UK is one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements for its citizens. Rather than just focusing on GDP, over 40 different sets of criteria from health, education and civil society engagement have been measured to get a more rounded assessment of how countries are performing.","locateZh":"一项最近的年度研究——考察各国把增长转化为福祉的能力——为上述问题带来一些启示。在所测的 163 国中,英国在确保经济增长转化为有意义的公民福祉方面表现垫底之一。该研究不是只盯 GDP,而是从健康、教育、公民社会参与等 40 多项指标入手,以得出更全面的评估。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文是 Across the 163 countries measured,163 国是被研究的对象;选项却说 sponsored by 163 countries(由 163 国资助),把 \"被测\" 偷换为 \"资助\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文是 Rather than just focusing on GDP, over 40 different sets of criteria…have been measured,强调 \"不只关注 GDP\" 而非完全排除;选项 excludes GDP as an indicator 把 \"不只\" 极化为 \"排除\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文反而强调 40 多项指标使评估更全面,作者持正面态度;Its criteria are questionable(指标值得质疑)与原文态度相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是 \"研究客观特征\";只有 Its results are enlightening 与 sheds some light on that question 直接呼应,锁 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"the UK is one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements for its citizens","opt":"Its results are enlightening"},{"orig":"sheds some light on that question","opt":"Its results are enlightening"}]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"In the last two paragraphs, the author suggests that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the UK is preparing for an economic boom."},{"key":"B","text":"high GDP foreshadows an economic decline."},{"key":"C","text":"it is essential to consider factors beyond GDP."},{"key":"D","text":"it requires caution to handle economic issues."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"在最后两段中,作者暗示____","choicesZh":{"A":"英国正在为经济繁荣做准备。","B":"高GDP预示着经济衰退。","C":"考虑GDP之外的因素是必要的。","D":"处理经济问题需要谨慎。"},"analysis":{"type":"the author suggests that____ 中 suggests 是推断题硬指标,答案要回到作者的议论而非具体细节。","parse":"In the last two paragraphs, the author suggests that____ 句首 In… 是地点状语限定证据范围,主干是 the author suggests that…,that 从句即选项补充内容。","locateEn":"So, what Kennedy was referring to was that while GDP has been the most common method for measuring the economic activity of nations, as a measure, it is no longer enough. It does not include important factors such as environmental quality or education outcomes – all things that contribute to a person's sense of well-being.","locateZh":"所以 Kennedy 当年所指的是:GDP 虽是衡量国家经济活动最常用的方法,但作为度量手段已经不够用了。它没有涵盖环境质量、教育成果等重要因素——而这些正是构成个人幸福感的来源。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"The sharp hit to growth predicted around the world and in the UK 明确预测经济急挫;选项却说英国 preparing for an economic boom(正在备战经济繁荣),与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"末两段没有把 GDP 高与经济衰退建立因果关系;high GDP foreshadows an economic decline(高 GDP 预示衰退)是凭空推断。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要 \"看 GDP 之外的因素\";只有 it is essential to consider factors beyond GDP 同时与 P6 和 P7 的议论吻合,锁 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"as a measure, it is no longer enough. It does not include important factors such as environmental quality or education outcomes","opt":"it is essential to consider factors beyond GDP"},{"orig":"policymakers who refocus efforts on improving well-being rather than simply worrying about GDP figures could avoid the forecasted doom","opt":"it is essential to consider factors beyond GDP"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"作者主张是把重心从 GDP 转到福祉,而非泛泛地 caution to handle economic issues(处理经济问题需谨慎);把鲜明的方向性主张稀释成普遍中性的 \"要谨慎\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"Which of the following is the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"High GDP But Inadequate Well-being, a UK Lesson"},{"key":"B","text":"GDP Figures, a Window on Global Economic Health"},{"key":"C","text":"Robert F. Kennedy, a Terminator of GDP"},{"key":"D","text":"Brexit, the UK's Gateway to Well-being"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"下列哪项是本文的最佳标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"GDP高但福祉不足,英国的教训","B":"GDP数据,观察全球经济健康状况的窗口","C":"Robert F. Kennedy,GDP的终结者","D":"Brexit,英国通往福祉的门户"},"analysis":{"type":"the best title for the text 标志这是覆盖全文的主旨题,需聚合各区间功能再选。","parse":"Which of the following is the best title for the text? 是 Which 引导的特殊疑问句,best title for the text 限定考察对象是全文标题。四个选项是名词短语+副标题样式,无语法陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"High GDP But Inadequate Well-being, a UK Lesson 同时含主线两要素(反差+英国教训),与各区间功能匹配最严,锁 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"the UK is one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements for its citizens","opt":"High GDP But Inadequate Well-being, a UK Lesson"},{"orig":"This is a lesson that rich countries can learn","opt":"a UK Lesson"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"全文核心是 GDP…is no longer enough,贬低 GDP 的覆盖力;选项 GDP Figures, a Window on Global Economic Health 反而把 GDP 包装成衡量全球经济健康的窗口,与作者立场相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"全文借 Kennedy 一句话开题,P1 之外几乎不再提他,更没说他 a Terminator of GDP(GDP 的终结者);把次要人物拔高为主角,且 Terminator 程度过重。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"P1、P2 只把 Brexit 当反思 GDP 的契机,作者并未说脱欧本身是 the UK's Gateway to Well-being(英国通向福祉的入口);把例证拔高为主旨。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"In a rare unanimous ruling, the US Supreme Court has overturned the corruption conviction of a former Virginia governor, Robert McDonnell. But it did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct, which included accepting gifts such as a Rolex watch and a Ferrari automobile from a company seeking access to government."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"The high court's decision said the judge in Mr. McDonnell's trial failed to tell a jury that it must look only at his \"official acts,\" or the former governor's decisions on \"specific\" and \"unsettled\" issues related to his duties."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"Merely helping a gift-giver gain access to other officials, unless done with clear intent to pressure those officials, is not corruption, the justices found."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"The court did suggest that accepting favors in return for opening doors is \"distasteful\" and \"nasty.\" But under anti-bribery laws, proof must be made of concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation. Simply arranging a meeting, making a phone call, or hosting an event is not an \"official act\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"The court's ruling is legally sound in defining a kind of favoritism that is not criminal. Elected leaders must be allowed to help supporters deal with bureaucratic problems without fear of prosecution for bribery. \"The basic compact underlying representative government,\" wrote Chief Justice John Roberts for the court, \"assumes that public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"But the ruling reinforces the need for citizens and their elected representatives, not the courts, to ensure equality of access to government. Officials must not be allowed to play favorites in providing information or in arranging meetings simply because an individual or group provides a campaign donation or a personal gift. This type of integrity requires well-enforced laws in government transparency, such as records of official meetings, rules on lobbying, and information about each elected leader's source of wealth."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"Favoritism in official access can fan public perceptions of corruption. But it is not always corruption. Rather officials must avoid double standards, or different types of access for average people and the wealthy. If connections can be bought, a basic premise of democratic society – that all are equal in treatment by government – is undermined. Good governance rests on an understanding of the inherent worth of each individual."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-8","text":"The court's ruling is a step forward in the struggle against both corruption and official favoritism."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"The underlined sentence (Para. 1) most probably shows that the court____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"avoided defining the extent of McDonnell's duties."},{"key":"B","text":"made no compromise in convicting McDonnell."},{"key":"C","text":"was contemptuous of McDonnell's conduct."},{"key":"D","text":"refused to comment on McDonnell's ethics."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"下划线句子(第1段)最有可能表明法院____","choicesZh":{"A":"避免界定McDonnell职责的范围。","B":"在定罪McDonnell时没有作出妥协。","C":"对McDonnell的行为持轻蔑态度。","D":"拒绝对McDonnell的道德操守发表评论。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The underlined sentence (Para. 1) most probably shows that 直接问下划线句最可能表达什么，是经典的句意理解题。","parse":"主干 The underlined sentence … most probably shows that the court ____，that 引导宾语从句，从句主语 the court，谓语待填；most probably 是程度状语，提示答案是合理推断而非绝对断言，不存在双重否定或比较结构，结构平铺无陷阱。","locateEn":"But it did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct, which included accepting gifts such as a Rolex watch and a Ferrari automobile from a company seeking access to government.","locateZh":"但法院如此判决时，是 \"捏着鼻子\" 看待他行为中的道德问题的——这些行为包括接受一家寻求接近政府的公司所赠的劳力士手表与法拉利轿车等礼物。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原句根本未提 \"职责范围\" 或对 duties 的界定问题，avoided defining the extent of McDonnell's duties 凭空捏造了一个动作对象。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原句明确说法院推翻了定罪（has overturned the corruption conviction），即并未 \"毫无妥协地定罪\"；made no compromise in convicting McDonnell 与事实完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"对其行为不齿\" 与 was contemptuous of McDonnell's conduct 完全对应，contemptuous 正是 hold one's nose at 的语义同义词。","pairs":[{"orig":"holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct","opt":"was contemptuous of McDonnell's conduct"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原句正是法院对 ethics 公开表态（捏鼻子嫌恶），并非 \"拒绝评价\"；refused to comment on McDonnell's ethics 与事实相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"According to Paragraph 4, an official act is deemed corruptive only if it involves____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"leaking secrets intentionally."},{"key":"B","text":"sizable gains in the form of gifts."},{"key":"C","text":"concrete returns for gift-givers."},{"key":"D","text":"breaking contracts officially."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第4段,官方行为只有在涉及____时才被视为腐败","choicesZh":{"A":"故意泄露机密。","B":"以礼物形式获得的巨额收益。","C":"为送礼者提供具体回报。","D":"正式违反合同。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to Paragraph 4, an official act is deemed corruptive only if it involves 是典型 According to … 句式，问的是段内事实条件。","parse":"an official act is deemed corruptive only if it involves ____，被动句 be deemed + 形容词，only if 引导唯一条件状语从句，involves 后接动名词/名词作宾语。only if 是唯一性限定，提示选项必须是 \"必要且充分\" 的条件，任何把可能条件当作充要条件的选项都要警惕。","locateEn":"But under anti-bribery laws, proof must be made of concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation.","locateZh":"但依据反贿赂法，必须证明存在具体的好处，例如批准某项合同或法规。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P4 通篇未提 \"泄密\" 或 secrets；leaking secrets intentionally 与文章核心议题 \"接触/会面/合同\" 完全不在同一语义场。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"sizable gains in the form of gifts 偷换了 \"benefits\" 的指向——原文 concrete benefits 指送礼者获得的具体好处（合同/法规获批），而 B 说的是 \"以礼物形式收到的大额收益\"，把回报对象从送礼者倒置成官员，且把 concrete（具体）偷换为 sizable（数额大）。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"存在具体回报\" 与 concrete returns for gift-givers 在限定词 concrete 与核心名词 returns 上均一一对应，是定位句的同义压缩。","pairs":[{"orig":"proof must be made of concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation","opt":"concrete returns for gift-givers"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 approval of a contract or regulation 强调的是 \"批准\" 合同——给出合同；breaking contracts officially 却说 \"官方撕毁合同\"，方向完全相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"The court's ruling is based on the assumption that public officials are____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"justified in addressing the needs of their constituents."},{"key":"B","text":"qualified to deal independently with bureaucratic issues."},{"key":"C","text":"allowed to focus on the concerns of their supporters."},{"key":"D","text":"exempt from conviction on the charge of favoritism."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"法院的裁决基于这样的假设:公职人员____","choicesZh":{"A":"有理由满足其选民的需求。","B":"有资格独立处理官僚事务。","C":"被允许关注其支持者的关切。","D":"免于因偏袒指控而被定罪。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干问的是判决背后的 assumption（潜在前提），不是字面写出的事实，需要从作者引用 Roberts 的话 The basic compact underlying representative government, … assumes that … 中推一步。","parse":"The court's ruling is based on the assumption that public officials are ____，that 引导同位语从句解释 assumption，从句主系表结构，表语待填；is based on the assumption that 是固定结构，提示空格内容必须是一个 \"被默认成立\" 的前提性陈述。","locateEn":"\"The basic compact underlying representative government,\" wrote Chief Justice John Roberts for the court, \"assumes that public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns.\"","locateZh":"首席大法官 John Roberts 代表法院写道：\"代议制政府所依据的基本契约假定，公职人员应当倾听选民的诉求并就其关切采取行动。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"回应选民正当\" 与 justified in addressing the needs of their constituents 在 \"正当\"（justified）与 \"回应选民需求\"（addressing the needs of their constituents）两点同时命中。","pairs":[{"orig":"public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns","opt":"justified in addressing the needs of their constituents"},{"orig":"their constituents","opt":"their constituents"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说官员应 hear from constituents and act on their concerns，并未说他们有能力/资格 \"独立\" 处理 bureaucratic 问题；qualified to deal independently with bureaucratic issues 加上的 qualified（有资格）和 independently（独立地）都是原文未给的限定。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文用的是 constituents（全体选民）；allowed to focus on the concerns of their supporters 把对象偷换成 supporters（支持者/拥趸），并加上 focus on（专注于）这种排他性动词，与原文 \"普惠选民\" 的语义场冲突——P7 反对的恰恰就是这种偏袒。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 \"在不担心被起诉贿赂罪的情况下\" 帮助选民处理问题，并未一概给官员 \"豁免偏袒罪\" 的特权；exempt from conviction on the charge of favoritism 把范围从 \"bribery 一项\" 推广到 \"favoritism 整体\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"Well-enforced laws in government transparency are needed to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"awaken the conscience of officials."},{"key":"B","text":"guarantee fair play in official access."},{"key":"C","text":"allow for certain kinds of lobbying."},{"key":"D","text":"inspire hopes in average people."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"需要严格执行政府透明度法律以____","choicesZh":{"A":"唤醒官员的良知。","B":"保证官方接触的公平性。","C":"允许某些类型的游说。","D":"激发普通民众的希望。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Well-enforced laws in government transparency are needed to ____ 问的是这套法律是为了实现什么功能，答案就在原文该短语前后，是客观事实题。","parse":"Well-enforced laws in government transparency are needed to ____，主语长名词短语，are needed to do 不定式作目的状语；待填部分是动词原形，要看选项动词与原文目的句的语义是否一致。","locateEn":"But the ruling reinforces the need for citizens and their elected representatives, not the courts, to ensure equality of access to government. Officials must not be allowed to play favorites in providing information or in arranging meetings simply because an individual or group provides a campaign donation or a personal gift. This type of integrity requires well-enforced laws in government transparency, such as records of official meetings, rules on lobbying, and information about each elected leader's source of wealth.","locateZh":"但这一判决强化了一种需要——由公民及其民选代表（而非法院）来确保接触政府的机会平等。官员决不能仅因为某个人或团体提供了竞选捐款或私人礼物，就在提供信息或安排会面上偏袒他们。这种正直要求在政府透明上拥有执行有力的法律，例如官方会议的记录、关于游说的规则，以及关于每位民选领导人财富来源的信息。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P6 全段未提 conscience（良心），原文谈的是制度性约束（laws/transparency/records），与 \"唤醒良心\" 这种道德感化路径完全不同；awaken the conscience of officials 凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"保障接触平等\" 与 guarantee fair play in official access 在 \"公平\"（fair play = equality）与 \"接触\"（official access = access to government）两点同时命中。","pairs":[{"orig":"to ensure equality of access to government","opt":"guarantee fair play in official access"},{"orig":"Officials must not be allowed to play favorites in providing information or in arranging meetings","opt":"fair play in official access"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文将 rules on lobbying 列为透明法律的 \"具体内容\"（即对游说立规约束）；allow for certain kinds of lobbying 把 \"立规约束\" 倒成了 \"允许某些游说\"，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"P6 未讨论 \"给普通民众带去希望\" 的情感效应；hopes 在原文无对应词，inspire hopes in average people 凭空生造。\"average people\" 出现于 different types of access for average people and the wealthy，但属于另一段对比，且并非透明法律的直接目的。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"The author's attitude toward the court's ruling is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sarcastic."},{"key":"B","text":"tolerant."},{"key":"C","text":"skeptical."},{"key":"D","text":"supportive."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对法院裁决的态度是____","choicesZh":{"A":"讽刺的。","B":"宽容的。","C":"怀疑的。","D":"支持的。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author's attitude toward the court's ruling is ____ 是经典态度题模板。","parse":"The author's attitude toward the court's ruling is ____，主系表结构，toward 短语限定态度对象；空格是形容词，须能匹配作者整体评价的极性与强度（正/负/中以及强弱）。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"sarcastic（讽刺的）要求作者表面褒实则贬；本文末段 a step forward 是真心正向定调，前文 legally sound 也是正面背书，没有反讽信号。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"tolerant（容忍的）暗示 \"勉强接受、心有不愿\"；但作者对判决是主动正向评价（legally sound + a step forward），并非 \"容忍\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"skeptical（怀疑的）要求作者对判决的正当性提出质疑；但作者明说判决 legally sound 并定调为 a step forward，没有质疑判决本身——他只是在判决之外建议补充透明法律，不构成对判决的怀疑。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"末段 a step forward 是显性正向定调，结合 legally sound 等理由句，作者立场清晰为 supportive，与预判 \"整体支持\" 完全对上。","pairs":[{"orig":"The court's ruling is a step forward in the struggle against both corruption and official favoritism","opt":"supportive"},{"orig":"The court's ruling is legally sound in defining a kind of favoritism that is not criminal","opt":"supportive"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"ordering","title":"Section II Part B 段落排序","directions":"Directions: The following paragraphs are given in a wrong order. For questions 41 -45, you are required to reorganize these paragraphs into a coherent text by choosing from the list A-G and filling them into the numbered boxes. Paragraphs B and D have been correctly placed. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","points":10,"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"A","text":"The first published sketch, \"A Dinner at Poplar Walk\" brought tears to Dickens's eyes when he discovered it in the pages of The Monthly Magazine. From then on his sketches, which appeared under the pen name \"Boz\" in The Evening Chronicle, earned him a modest reputation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"B","text":"The runaway success of The Pickwick Papers, as it is generally known today, secured Dickens's fame. There were Pickwick coats and Pickwick cigars, and the plump, spectacled hero, Samuel Pickwick, became a national figure."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"C","text":"Soon after Sketches by Boz appeared, a publishing firm approached Dickens to write a story in monthly installments, as a backdrop for a series of woodcuts by the then-famous artist Robert Seymour, who had originated the idea for the story. With characteristic confidence, Dickens successfully insisted that Seymour's pictures illustrate his own story instead. After the first installment, Dickens wrote to the artist and asked him to correct a drawing Dickens felt was not faithful enough to his prose. Seymour made the change, went into his backyard, and expressed his displeasure by committing suicide. Dickens and his publishers simply pressed on with a new artist. The comic novel, The Posthumous Papers of the Pickwick Club, appeared serially in 1836 and 1837 and was first published in book form in 1837."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"D","text":"Charles Dickens is probably the best-known and, to many people, the greatest English novelist of the 19th century. A moralist, satirist, and social reformer, Dickens crafted complex plots and striking characters that capture the panorama of English society."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"E","text":"Soon after his father's release from prison, Dickens got a better job as errand boy in law offices. He taught himself shorthand to get an even better job later as a court stenographer and as a reporter in Parliament. At the same time, Dickens, who had a reporter's eye for transcribing the life around him, especially anything comic or odd, submitted short sketches to obscure magazines."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"F","text":"Dickens was born in Portsmouth, on England's southern coast. His father was a clerk in the British Navy pay office – a respectable position, but with little social status. His paternal grandparents, a steward and a housekeeper, possessed even less status, having been servants, and Dickens later concealed their background. Dickens's mother supposedly came from a more respectable family. Yet two years before Dickens's birth, his mother's father was caught stealing and fled to Europe, never to return. The family's increasing poverty forced Dickens out of school at age 12 to work in Warren's Blacking Warehouse, a shoe-polish factory, where the other working boys mocked him as \"the young gentleman.\" His father was then imprisoned for debt. The humiliations of his father's imprisonment and his labor in the blacking factory formed Dickens's greatest wound and became his deepest secret. He could not confide them even to his wife, although they provide the unacknowledged foundation of his fiction."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"G","text":"After Pickwick, Dickens plunged into a bleaker world. In Oliver Twist, he traces an orphan's progress from the workhouse to the criminal slums of London. Nicholas Nickleby, his next novel, combines the darkness of Oliver Twist with the sunlight of Pickwick. The popularity of these novels consolidated Dickens as a nationally and internationally celebrated man of letters."}],"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"The first published sketch, \"A Dinner at Poplar Walk\" brought tears to Dickens's eyes when he discovered it in the pages of The Monthly Magazine. From then on his sketches, which appeared under the pen name \"Boz\" in The Evening Chronicle, earned him a modest reputation."},{"key":"B","text":"The runaway success of The Pickwick Papers, as it is generally known today, secured Dickens's fame. There were Pickwick coats and Pickwick cigars, and the plump, spectacled hero, Samuel Pickwick, became a national figure."},{"key":"C","text":"Soon after Sketches by Boz appeared, a publishing firm approached Dickens to write a story in monthly installments, as a backdrop for a series of woodcuts by the then-famous artist Robert Seymour, who had originated the idea for the story. With characteristic confidence, Dickens successfully insisted that Seymour's pictures illustrate his own story instead. After the first installment, Dickens wrote to the artist and asked him to correct a drawing Dickens felt was not faithful enough to his prose. Seymour made the change, went into his backyard, and expressed his displeasure by committing suicide. Dickens and his publishers simply pressed on with a new artist. The comic novel, The Posthumous Papers of the Pickwick Club, appeared serially in 1836 and 1837 and was first published in book form in 1837."},{"key":"D","text":"Charles Dickens is probably the best-known and, to many people, the greatest English novelist of the 19th century. A moralist, satirist, and social reformer, Dickens crafted complex plots and striking characters that capture the panorama of English society."},{"key":"E","text":"Soon after his father's release from prison, Dickens got a better job as errand boy in law offices. He taught himself shorthand to get an even better job later as a court stenographer and as a reporter in Parliament. At the same time, Dickens, who had a reporter's eye for transcribing the life around him, especially anything comic or odd, submitted short sketches to obscure magazines."},{"key":"F","text":"Dickens was born in Portsmouth, on England's southern coast. His father was a clerk in the British Navy pay office – a respectable position, but with little social status. His paternal grandparents, a steward and a housekeeper, possessed even less status, having been servants, and Dickens later concealed their background. Dickens's mother supposedly came from a more respectable family. Yet two years before Dickens's birth, his mother's father was caught stealing and fled to Europe, never to return. The family's increasing poverty forced Dickens out of school at age 12 to work in Warren's Blacking Warehouse, a shoe-polish factory, where the other working boys mocked him as \"the young gentleman.\" His father was then imprisoned for debt. The humiliations of his father's imprisonment and his labor in the blacking factory formed Dickens's greatest wound and became his deepest secret. He could not confide them even to his wife, although they provide the unacknowledged foundation of his fiction."},{"key":"G","text":"After Pickwick, Dickens plunged into a bleaker world. In Oliver Twist, he traces an orphan's progress from the workhouse to the criminal slums of London. Nicholas Nickleby, his next novel, combines the darkness of Oliver Twist with the sunlight of Pickwick. The popularity of these novels consolidated Dickens as a nationally and internationally celebrated man of letters."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"F"},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"E"},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"A"},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"C"},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"G"}],"order":["D","F","E","A","C","B","G"],"fixed":{"0":"D","5":"B"},"chain":"D → 41. → 42. → 43. → 44. → B → 45.","orderChain":"正确顺序 预给 D → 41 F → 42 E → 43 A → 44 C → 预给 B → 45 G","seams":["【承接前一段】 段 D 词汇复现：D 用全名总评后，F 接着只用姓氏从「出生」讲起 。given 段 D 以全名 Charles Dickens 做完总评，F 段首即 Dickens was born in Portsmouth，只用姓氏、从出生写起——这是传记「总评→出身」的标准接缝，F 紧跟 D。","【承接前一段】 段 F 指代衔接：E 段首「父亲出狱」精确回指 F 段尾「父亲入狱」 。F 段尾 His father was then imprisoned for debt 写父亲入狱，E 段首 Soon after his father's release from prison 紧接写父亲出狱。release from prison 唯一能消解到的就是 F 的 imprisoned for debt，时间上「入狱→出狱」严丝合缝，把 E 钉在 F 后。","【承接前一段】 段 E 词汇复现：A 的「第一篇 sketch」复现并承接 E 的「投稿 short sketches」 。E 段尾 submitted short sketches to obscure magazines 写他开始投稿 sketch，A 段首 The first published sketch 紧接写其中第一篇刊出。sketch 一词复现，且「投稿（泛指多篇）→第一篇见报」逻辑顺承，A 紧跟 E。","【承接前一段】 段 A 词汇复现：C 段首的《Sketches by Boz》复现 A 铺出的 Boz 笔名 。A 段写他以笔名 \"Boz\" 投稿成集，C 段首 Soon after Sketches by Boz appeared 紧接以《Sketches by Boz》出版为起点。Boz 一词复现、且「成集→出版后被约稿」逻辑顺承，C 紧跟 A。","【引出后一段】 段 B 词汇复现：C 写《匹克威克》成书，B 紧接写它大获成功 。C 段尾把 The Posthumous Papers of the Pickwick Club 写到出版成书，given 段 B 段首即 The runaway success of The Pickwick Papers，复现这部书并续写其成功。C 落在 B（given）之前，与卷面 given 完全吻合，双侧夹证。","【承接前一段】 段 B 词汇复现：G 段首 After Pickwick 直接承接 B 写就的《匹克威克》成功 。given 段 B 段首 The runaway success of The Pickwick Papers 写这部书大获成功，G 段首 After Pickwick, Dickens plunged into a bleaker world 以 After Pickwick 续写成名之后的转向。Pickwick 复现、「成名→此后题材转阴郁」顺承，G 紧跟 B，且为全文收尾段。"]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"The growth of the use of English as the world's primary language for international communication has obviously been continuing for several decades. (46) But even as the number of English speakers expands further there are signs that the global predominance of the language may fade within the foreseeable future."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"Complex international, economic, technological and cultural changes could start to diminish the leading position of English as the language of the world market, and UK interests which enjoy advantage from the breadth of English usage would consequently face new pressures. Those realistic possibilities are highlighted in the study presented by David Graddol. (47) His analysis should therefore end any self-contentedness among those who may believe that the global position of English is so stable that the young generations of the United Kingdom do not need additional language capabilities."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"David Graddol concludes that monoglot English graduates face a bleak economic future as qualified multilingual youngsters from other countries are proving to have a competitive advantage over their British counterparts in global companies and organisations. Alongside that, (48) many countries are introducing English into the primary-school curriculum but British schoolchildren and students do not appear to be gaining greater encouragement to achieve fluency in other languages."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-4","text":"If left to themselves, such trends will diminish the relative strength of the English language in international education markets as the demand for educational resources in languages, such as Spanish, Arabic or Mandarin grows and international business process outsourcing in other languages such as Japanese, French and German, spreads."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-5","text":"(49) The changes identified by David Graddol all present clear and major challenges to the UK's providers of English language teaching to people of other countries and to broader education business sectors. The English language teaching sector directly earns nearly ￡1.3 billion for the UK in invisible exports and our other education related exports earn up to ￡10 billion a year more. As the international education market expands, the recent slowdown in the numbers of international students studying in the main English-speaking countries is likely to continue, especially if there are no effective strategic policies to prevent such slippage."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-6","text":"The anticipation of possible shifts in demand provided by this study is significant: (50) It gives a basis to all organisations which seek to promote the learning and use of English, a basis for planning to meet the possibilities of what could be a very different operating environment. That is a necessary and practical approach. In this as in much else, those who wish to influence the future must prepare for it."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"But even as the number of English speakers expands further there are signs that the global predominance of the language may fade within the foreseeable future.","refZh":"但是，即便说英语的人数进一步增长，仍有迹象表明：英语在全球的主导地位可能会在可预见的未来逐渐式微。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"But even as the number of English speakers expands further","lit":"但即使说英语的人数进一步增长","role":"（让步状语从句（even as 引导））","note":"难点： even as = 即便在……的同时 even as 是固定搭配，表「即使在……之时/尽管」，引导让步，不要拆成 even（甚至）+ as（当）。它与后半句的 But 呼应，构成「虽然人数在涨，但地位可能降」的转折让步，是本句逻辑骨架，对应 even as the number of English speakers expands further。"},{"en":"there are signs that","lit":"有迹象表明","role":"（主句主干（there be 句型））","note":"难点： signs that 后接同位语从句 that 在此不是定语从句，而是引导同位语从句、解释 signs 的具体内容，译成「有迹象表明/有迹象显示……」，that 本身不译出。"},{"en":"the global predominance of the language may fade","lit":"这门语言的全球主导地位可能会衰落","role":"（同位语从句主干）","note":"难点： predominance＝主导/支配地位；the language 回指 English predominance 是抽象名词，意为「主导地位、支配地位、优势地位」，不要望文译成「预测」（与 predict 无关）。fade 本义「褪色」，此处具体化为「衰退、减弱、式微」。the language 按第一步锚定还原为「英语」，对应 the global predominance of the language may fade。"},{"en":"within the foreseeable future.","lit":"在可预见的未来之内","role":"（时间状语）","note":"难点： foreseeable＝可预见的 foreseeable 由 foresee（预见）+ -able 构成，within the foreseeable future 是固定表达「在可预见的未来/不久的将来」。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"His analysis should therefore end any self-contentedness among those who may believe that the global position of English is so stable that the young generations of the United Kingdom do not need additional language capabilities.","refZh":"因此，他的分析理应终结某些人的自满情绪：这些人可能认为，英语的全球地位如此稳固，以至于英国的年轻一代根本无需再掌握其他语言能力。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"His analysis should therefore end any self-contentedness","lit":"因此他的分析应当终结任何自满情绪","role":"（主句主干（主谓宾））","note":"难点： self-contentedness＝自满/自鸣得意 self-contentedness 由 self（自我）+ contented（满足的）+ -ness（名词后缀）构成，意为「自满、自鸣得意」，带贬义，呼应全文「英国不该高枕无忧」的基调。His 指 David Graddol 的，可译「他的分析」或点明「Graddol 的分析」。end 此处取「结束、终结、打消」。"},{"en":"among those who may believe that","lit":"在那些可能认为……的人当中","role":"（介词短语＋who 定语从句）","note":"难点： those who 套 that 宾语从句 those who may believe＝「那些可能认为/相信……的人」，who 引导定语从句修饰 those；believe 后的 that 引导宾语从句、交代他们相信的内容。译时把「那些……的人」整体作为 self-contentedness 的归属者。"},{"en":"the global position of English is so stable that","lit":"英语的全球地位如此稳固，以至于","role":"（so...that 结果状语从句的前半（原因））","note":"难点： so...that＝如此……以至于 本句是 believe that [ ...so stable that... ] 的双层 that。第二个 that 与前面的 so 构成 so...that「如此……以至于」结果结构，不要漏掉「以至于」这层因果。the global position of English 即「英语的全球地位」，术语与全文统一。"},{"en":"the young generations of the United Kingdom do not need additional language capabilities.","lit":"英国的年轻一代不需要额外的语言能力","role":"（so...that 结果从句的后半（结果））","note":"难点： additional language capabilities＝（英语之外）额外的语言能力 additional 指「英语之外另加的」，capabilities 在此是「能力、本领」；联系全文 the young generations of the United Kingdom do not need additional language capabilities，即英国年轻人无需再学其他外语，呼应第 48 句「英国学生不被鼓励学外语」。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"many countries are introducing English into the primary-school curriculum but British schoolchildren and students do not appear to be gaining greater encouragement to achieve fluency in other languages.","refZh":"许多国家正在将英语纳入小学课程，但英国的中小学生及学生似乎并未得到更多鼓励去熟练掌握其他语言。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"many countries are introducing English into the primary-school curriculum","lit":"许多国家正在把英语引入小学课程","role":"（前一并列分句（主谓宾））","note":"难点： introduce ... into＝把……引入；curriculum＝课程（体系） introduce 在此不是「介绍」而是「引进、纳入」，introduce English into the curriculum＝「把英语纳入课程」；curriculum 指「（学校的）课程、教学大纲」，primary-school curriculum 即「小学课程」。这是熟词僻义高发点。"},{"en":"but British schoolchildren and students","lit":"但英国的中小学生和大学生","role":"（后一并列分句主语（but 转折））","note":"难点： schoolchildren and students＝（中小学）学生与（大学）学生 but 标记与前句的对比转折；schoolchildren 指学龄儿童/中小学生，students 泛指学生（含大学生），两词并列可合译为「英国的中小学生及学生」。"},{"en":"do not appear to be gaining greater encouragement","lit":"似乎并没有得到更多的鼓励","role":"（谓语（含否定＋appear to））","note":"难点： do not appear to＝似乎并没有（含蓄否定的语序） 否定词 not 在 appear 上，但语义上否定的是后面「得到鼓励」，英语习惯说 do not appear to be gaining＝「似乎并未得到」，译时把否定落到「得到」上读着才顺；greater encouragement＝「更多/更大的鼓励」。"},{"en":"to achieve fluency in other languages.","lit":"去熟练掌握其他语言","role":"（不定式作目的状语）","note":"难点： achieve fluency in＝（在某语言上）达到流利/熟练掌握 fluency 是抽象名词「流利、流畅」，achieve fluency in other languages 直译「在其他语言上达到流利」读着生硬，宜具体化为「熟练掌握/学好其他语言」。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"The changes identified by David Graddol all present clear and major challenges to the UK's providers of English language teaching to people of other countries and to broader education business sectors.","refZh":"David Graddol 所指出的这些变化，全都给英国那些向他国民众提供英语教学的机构、以及更广泛的教育产业部门带来了明确而重大的挑战。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The changes identified by David Graddol","lit":"由 David Graddol 所指出的这些变化","role":"（主语＋过去分词后置定语）","note":"难点： identified by＝被……识别/指出（过去分词作后置定语） identified by David Graddol 是过去分词短语作后置定语修饰 The changes，相当于 which were identified by…；identify 此处取「识别、指出、发现」。这些 changes 按第一步锚定即前文 Graddol 研究揭示的那些趋势。"},{"en":"all present clear and major challenges","lit":"全都构成了明确而重大的挑战","role":"（谓语＋宾语（all 同位强调））","note":"难点： present 此处＝带来/构成；all 修饰主语 present 是熟词僻义高发点，此处不是「呈现/礼物」，而是「提出、带来、构成」（present challenges to＝「给……带来挑战」）；all 紧跟主语，强调「这些变化全都」带来挑战。"},{"en":"to the UK's providers of English language teaching to people of other countries","lit":"对英国向他国民众提供英语教学的机构而言","role":"（介词短语作状语（challenges 的承受方一））","note":"难点： providers of English language teaching to people of other countries＝向他国人民提供英语教学的（机构） 这是多重 of/to 套叠的难点：providers（提供者/机构）of English language teaching（英语教学）to people of other countries（面向他国民众）。要顺着「向他国民众 → 提供英语教学 → 的机构」理顺修饰链，对应 the UK's providers of English language teaching to people of other countries。"},{"en":"and to broader education business sectors.","lit":"以及更广泛的教育产业部门","role":"（并列介词短语（承受方二））","note":"难点： broader education business sectors＝更广义的教育产业/商业部门 and to… 与前一个 to 并列，是 challenges 的第二个承受对象；broader＝「更广泛的」，education business sectors＝「教育商业/产业部门」。两个 to 并列，说明挑战同时冲击「英语教学机构」和「更广的教育产业」。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"It gives a basis to all organisations which seek to promote the learning and use of English, a basis for planning to meet the possibilities of what could be a very different operating environment.","refZh":"这项研究为所有致力于推广英语学习与使用的机构提供了一个依据，一个据以制定规划、从而应对未来那种可能截然不同的运营环境及其种种可能性的依据。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"It gives a basis to all organisations","lit":"它为所有机构提供了一个基础","role":"（主句主干（主谓双宾））","note":"难点： It 回指上句的 this study（这项研究） 句首 It 须按第一步锚定还原：回指上一句 The anticipation of possible shifts in demand provided by this study，即「这项研究（对需求变化的预判）」。孤立译成「它」会断链，应顺承译为「这项研究为……提供了基础」。basis＝「基础、依据」。"},{"en":"which seek to promote the learning and use of English,","lit":"（这些机构）致力于推广英语的学习和使用","role":"（which 引导的定语从句（修饰 organisations））","note":"难点： seek to＝力图/致力于；promote＝推广/促进 which 修饰 all organisations；seek to do＝「设法、力求、致力于做」；promote 取「推广、促进」；the learning and use of English＝「英语的学习与使用」。即「致力于推广英语学习与使用的（所有机构）」。"},{"en":"a basis for planning to meet the possibilities","lit":"一个用以规划、以应对种种可能性的基础","role":"（同位语（重复 a basis 作补充说明））","note":"难点： a basis 是前一个 a basis 的同位语；meet＝应对 逗号后的 a basis 与前面的 a basis 同位，进一步说明这个「基础」是干什么用的；for planning to meet…＝「用于规划以应对……」；meet 此处熟词僻义，取「应对、迎接（挑战/可能性）」而非「遇见」。"},{"en":"of what could be a very different operating environment.","lit":"（应对）可能会是一种迥然不同的运营环境（所带来的种种可能）","role":"（of＋what 引导的宾语从句作定语）","note":"难点： what could be＝可能会是的（那种情形）；operating environment＝运营/经营环境 what could be a very different operating environment 是 of 的宾语从句，what 引导，意为「可能会是一种全然不同的运营环境的（局面）」；could be 是虚拟/推测语气「可能会成为」；operating environment＝「运营环境、经营环境」。它与前面的 the possibilities 连读：应对「一种可能截然不同的运营环境」所带来的各种可能性。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: You are to write an email to James Cook, a newly-arrived Australian professor, recommending some tourist attractions in your city. Please give reasons for your recommendation. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end of the email. Use “Li Ming” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: You are to write an email to James Cook, a newly-arrived Australian professor, recommending some tourist attractions in your city. Please give reasons for your recommendation. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end of the email. Use “Li Ming” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear James, Warm welcome to our city! As you have just arrived, I am writing to recommend two attractions that I believe you will love. The first is the Great Wall. Winding over the mountains, it offers breathtaking views and a vivid lesson in Chinese history, which should fascinate you as a scholar. The second is the Palace Museum, where thousands of imperial treasures reveal our ancient culture and craftsmanship. Both places are easy to reach and rewarding. I am sure they will make your stay memorable. Feel free to contact me if you need a guide. Yours, Li Ming","translation":"亲爱的 James：\n热烈欢迎你来到我们的城市！你刚刚抵达，我写这封邮件是想向你推荐两处我相信你会喜欢的景点。\n第一处是长城。它蜿蜒于群山之上，风光壮丽震撼，也是了解中国历史的生动一课——作为一名学者，你想必会为之着迷。第二处是故宫，那里珍藏着成千上万件皇家文物，展现着我们古老的文化与精湛的工艺。\n这两处都交通便利、收获满满。我相信它们会让你在这里的日子难以忘怀。若你需要向导，尽管联系我。\n此致 李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"开场点题","text":"【第 1 段】 开场点题 。首段用 Warm welcome to our city! 拉近距离，紧接 I am writing to recommend two attractions... 落实『开门见山表目的』，一句欢迎一句来意，直接对上 recommending some tourist attractions in your city。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"两景两因","text":"【第 2 段】 两景两因 。The first is the Great Wall... which should fascinate you as a scholar 与 The second is the Palace Museum, where... reveal our ancient culture and craftsmanship 把『一景一因分点写』落地，每处景点后都紧跟理由，满足 Please give reasons for your recommendation。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"邀约收尾并落款","text":"【第 3 段】 邀约收尾并落款 。Both places are easy to reach... 总评收束，Feel free to contact me if you need a guide 主动提供帮助，末尾 Li Ming 满足 Do not sign your own name at the end of the email。"}],"wordCount":100}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following pictures. In your essay, you should 1）describe the pictures briefly, 2）interpret the meaning, and 3）give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following pictures. In your essay, you should 1）describe the pictures briefly, 2）interpret the meaning, and 3）give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2017-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅由左右两部分组成的漫画","width":"652","height":"538","local":"assets/writing/2017-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the two pictures, a striking contrast is presented. In the left one, a man leans back in his chair with a relaxed look, surrounded by shelves crammed with books, saying \"I own so many books.\" In the right one, another man sits at his desk, smiling as he reads, and declares, \"I will strive to finish reading twenty books this year.\" Simple as it seems, the cartoon conveys a thought-provoking message. The first man symbolizes those who take pride merely in possessing books, mistaking ownership for knowledge, while the second represents people who set concrete goals and translate intention into real action. What truly enriches the mind is not how many books sit on our shelves, but how many we genuinely read and digest. As far as I am concerned, the latter attitude deserves our applause. Collecting books without reading them is nothing but self-deception, whereas a modest yet achievable reading plan can steadily broaden our horizons. Therefore, we young people should stop showing off our bookshelves and instead pick up a book, page by page, turning good intentions into lasting habits.","translation":"如两幅图所生动描绘的，呈现出鲜明的对比。左图中，一个人靠在椅子上，神情轻松，身后书架摆满了书，他说：“我拥有这么多书。”右图中，另一个人端坐书桌前，微笑着读书，他宣告：“我争取今年读完二十本书。”\n看似简单，这幅漫画却传递着发人深省的信息。前一个人象征那些仅仅以拥有书籍为傲、误把占有当作学问的人；后一个人则代表那些设定具体目标、把意愿化为实际行动的人。真正充实心灵的，不是书架上摆了多少书，而是我们真正读了、消化了多少。\n在我看来，后一种态度值得我们赞赏。藏书而不读，不过是自欺欺人；而一个虽不宏大却切实可行的阅读计划，能稳步开阔我们的眼界。因此，我们青年人应当不再炫耀书架，而是拿起一本书，一页页读下去，把美好的意愿变成长久的习惯。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"总起＋左右白描","text":"【第 1 段】 总起＋左右白描 。用 As is vividly depicted in the two pictures 总起点出对比，再以 In the left one / In the right one 平行还原两幅画面，并原样引出两句对话框内容，只描述不评价，落实了描述段'客观白描、不抢戏'的功能。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"象征对照＋抽出道理","text":"【第 2 段】 象征对照＋抽出道理 。The first man symbolizes... while the second represents... 把两个人物对号到两类人，再用 What truly enriches the mind is not... but... 抽出'占有≠收获'的核心道理，点明讽刺与赞扬对象，落实寓意段'由物及理'的采分核心。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"亮立场＋给对策","text":"【第 3 段】 亮立场＋给对策 。以 As far as I am concerned 亮明支持'行动'一方，用 is nothing but... whereas... 对比给出理由，末句 Therefore, we young people should... turning... into... 落到可操作的呼吁，实现评论段'亮立场、给对策'的收尾。"}],"wordCount":187}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 B Besides · 2 A connected · 3 D host · 4 C avoid · 5 B involving · 6 D on · 7 B exposed · 8 C down · 9 A calculated · 10 D explained · 11 A Even · 12 B symptoms · 13 D increased · 14 B associated · 15 C generate · 16 A in the face of · 17 C attribute · 18 A because · 19 C remains · 20 D influences \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 A · 22 C · 23 D · 24 D · 25 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 B · 27 A · 28 B · 29 A · 30 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 D · 32 B · 33 D · 34 C · 35 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 C · 37 C · 38 A · 39 B · 40 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"段落排序 Section II Part B 预给D → 41=F → 42=E → 43=A → 44=C → 预给B → 45=G \n（逐题解析见 段落排序解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
